Pergunta do desenvolvedor:
Como configurar o SecurityFilterChain no Spring Boot 3.x com a remoção do WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter?

Resposta técnica fundamentada exclusivamente no contexto acima (incluindo citações):

No Spring Boot 3.x (Spring Security 6.x), a classe `WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter` foi completamente removida. As regras de segurança devem ser configuradas declarando um `@Bean` do tipo `SecurityFilterChain` usando a DSL baseada em lambdas e métodos de componentes:

```java
package com.example.demo.security;

import org.springframework.context.annotation.Bean;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Configuration;
import org.springframework.security.config.Customizer;
import org.springframework.security.config.annotation.web.builders.HttpSecurity;
import org.springframework.security.config.annotation.web.configuration.EnableWebSecurity;
import org.springframework.security.web.SecurityFilterChain;

@Configuration
@EnableWebSecurity
public class SecurityConfiguration {

    @Bean
    public SecurityFilterChain securityFilterChain(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {
        http
            .authorizeHttpRequests(authorize -> authorize
                .requestMatchers("/public/**", "/actuator/health").permitAll()
                .anyRequest().authenticated()
            )
            .httpBasic(Customizer.withDefaults())
            .csrf(csrf -> csrf.disable());
        return http.build();
    }
}
```

[Fonte: Configuring SecurityFilterChain (https://docs.spring.io/spring-boot/reference/web/spring-security.html)]

